# GharUrja Global Rules

You are building GharUrja.

Prioritize:

1. Trust.
2. Simplicity.
3. Performance.
4. Revenue generation.

---

## Architecture Rules

- Use Next.js App Router.
- Use TypeScript.
- Prefer server components when appropriate.
- Avoid unnecessary client-side JavaScript.
- Prefer static generation for SEO pages.

---

## Coding Rules

- Write clean, production-ready code.
- Favor readability over cleverness.
- Keep functions small.
- Separate business logic from UI logic.
- Avoid duplicate logic.
- Use descriptive naming.

---

## Product Rules

Do NOT build:

- User authentication.
- Installer dashboards.
- CRM systems.
- Payment processing.
- Overengineered admin systems.

Build ONLY features that support:

- SEO.
- AdSense revenue.
- Lead generation.
- User trust.

---

## Calculator Rules

- Display assumptions clearly.
- Use conservative estimates.
- Never present estimates as guarantees.
- Keep formulas centralized.
- Avoid hardcoded subsidy values.

---

## SEO Rules

- Prioritize long-tail keywords.
- Prioritize state-specific pages.
- Use internal linking.
- Avoid keyword stuffing.
- Prefer helpful content over generic content.

---

## UX Rules

- Design mobile-first.
- Keep forms short.
- Avoid unnecessary animations.
- Optimize for clarity.
- Use strong calls-to-action.

---

## Performance Rules

- Optimize images.
- Minimize JavaScript bundles.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Prefer static rendering when possible.

---

## Business Rules

Every feature must support one or more of:

- Traffic.
- Trust.
- Ad revenue.
- Qualified leads.

If not, defer the feature.
